  "$comment": [
    "Published test vectors for the primitives `sealedbox.py` implements. These are what pin its",
    "correctness: a round-trip test passes for a wrong-but-self-consistent implementation, so it",
    "proves nothing on its own.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE, per group:",
    "  x25519         RFC 7748 §5.2 (two single-scalar-multiplication vectors).",
    "  x25519Exchange RFC 7748 §6.1 (the Alice/Bob Diffie-Hellman example).",
    "  poly1305       RFC 8439 §2.5.2 ('Cryptographic Forum Research Group').",
    "  cryptoBox      The NaCl reference `crypto_box` vector from the distribution's tests/box.c,",
    "                 with the intermediate HSalsa20-derived shared key from tests/box7.c. It pins",
    "                 the whole stack at once: X25519 agreement, HSalsa20 key derivation, XSalsa20",
    "                 keystream, the 32-byte one-time-key reservation and the tag-first layout.",
    "",
    "All values are lowercase hex."
  ],
